            <ArticleTitle>Diagnosis and treatment of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000521995.38311.e7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) is a neurobehavioral disorder characterized by signs and symptoms of inattention, hyperactivity, and impulsivity that typically begin in childhood. ADHD can persist into adulthood, causing impairments in occupational performance and peer and family relationships. This article reviews the epidemiology, diagnosis, and treatment of ADHD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
